===Etymology 2===
Lower case form of upper case roman numeral [[C]], a standardization of {{m|mul|Ɔ}} and {{m|mul|C}} because the latter happens to be an abbreviation of {{der|mul|la|centum||hundred}}, from abbreviation of ƆIC, an alternative form of >I<, from tally stick markings resembling {{m|mul||Ж}} (a superimposed {{m|mul|X}} and {{m|mul|I}}), from the practice of designating each tenth X notch with an extra cut.

